<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms for using St. George Elite Fence: the referral service, the SMS program, STOP and HELP, age limit, independent companies and liability."
  path="/terms-of-service/"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  h1="Terms of Service"
  lede="The rules for using this site and our referral service, including our text-message program."
  reviewed="2026-09-26"
  reviewedLabel="September 26, 2026"
>
  <h2 id="acceptance">Agreement to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply to {site.domain} and to the referral service offered through it by {site.brandName}, operated by
    {site.legalEntity} ("we," "us"). By using the site or sending us a request, you agree to these terms and to our
    <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="age">You must be 18 or older</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least 18 years old to send a request, to join our text-message program, or otherwise use the referral service.
  </p>

  <h2 id="the-service">What the service is</h2>
  <p>
    {site.brandName} is a referral and matching service. We publish information about fence and block-wall projects and, at
    your request, pass your project details to an independent fence or wall company that covers your area. We are not a
    contractor. We do not build, install, or repair fences or walls, we do not employ or supervise the companies we refer you to,
    and we are not a party to any agreement you make with them. The price, scope, schedule, permits, workmanship, warranty,
    licensing, and insurance for any project are between you and the company you hire.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sms-program">SMS program terms</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Program description.</strong> If you check the consent box on our request form, you agree to receive text messages
    from {site.brandName} and from the independent company you are matched with about the request you submitted, such as a
    confirmation that we received it, which company will contact you, and follow-up about scheduling or a quote. We do not send
    promotional or marketing texts.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Message frequency varies</strong> with your request, usually a few messages.</li>
    <li><strong>Message and data rates may apply</strong>, according to your mobile plan.</li>
    <li><strong>To stop</strong>, reply STOP to any message. You will receive one confirmation and no further texts about that request.</li>
    <li><strong>For help</strong>, reply HELP to any message or use our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent is optional.</strong> You do not have to agree to receive texts to submit a request or to hire any company.</li>
    <li><strong>Carriers are not liable</strong> for delayed or undelivered messages.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    How we handle your number and consent is described in the <a href="/privacy-policy/#sms">SMS section of our Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="consent-to-contact">Consent to be contacted</h2>
  <p>
    When you send a request, you ask us and the company we match you with to contact you about it at the phone number or email
    you provide, using the methods you agreed to. You can withdraw consent at any time by replying STOP, telling the caller, or
    contacting us.
  </p>

  <h2 id="calls">Phone calls</h2>
  <p>
    Calls to a phone number on this site may be routed to us or to a matched company and may be logged or recorded as described
    in our <a href="/privacy-policy/#call-recording">Privacy Policy</a>. If a call is recorded, you will hear a notice at the start.
  </p>

  <h2 id="information">Information on this site</h2>
  <p>
    Our guides are general information, not legal, engineering, or professional advice. Cost ranges are planning estimates from
    dated, named sources, not quotes. City codes change, and the city or county and your HOA have the final word on what applies
    to your property. Confirm permits, property lines, utilities (call 811 before digging), and HOA rules before any work begins.
  </p>

  <h2 id="independent-companies">Independent companies</h2>
  <p>
    We do not guarantee the availability, pricing, licensing, insurance, workmanship, or conduct of any company we refer you to or
    mention on this site. Before you hire anyone, verify their Utah contractor license status with the Utah Division of Professional
    Licensing, confirm their insurance, and get the scope and price in writing. See
    <a href="/licensed-fence-contractor-compare-st-george-ut/">how to check a Utah contractor's license</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">No warranty and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site and the referral service are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, to the fullest
    extent the law allows. To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential
    damages, or for any loss arising from work performed, or not performed, by any company you hire. Some jurisdictions do not
    allow certain limitations, so some of these may not apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Do not submit false requests, requests on behalf of someone else without their permission, or content that is unlawful or
    abusive, and do not try to disrupt or scrape the site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="content">Content ownership</h2>
  <p>
    The guides, text, and design of this site belong to {site.legalEntity}. You may share links to them and quote short passages
    with attribution; please do not republish whole pages.
  </p>

  <h2 id="governing-law">Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Utah, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The "last reviewed" date above shows the latest version; continued use of the site after a change
    means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms can be sent through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
